    "narrative": "The offensive core for LawDog today is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (81.48) and **Bryce Harper** (80.21), both of whom benefit from highly favorable matchups against back-end starters. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is the standout play, as he exploits a soft matchup against Merrill Kelly (5.13 xERA) and draws an 8% boost for his prime spot in the two-hole. **Bryce Harper** rounds into form with a massive 16% park factor uplift, making him the safest bet for power production. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) provides the most exciting ceiling play; he is firing on all cylinders with a 13% platoon edge and a park factor bump that makes him an essential start against Kevin Montero. **Masyn Winn** (66.60) remains a high-floor selection for our SB-starved squad, as the matchup against a lumbering Max Scherzer (5.72 xERA) and a perceived slow delivery provides him a green light on the basepaths.\n\nOur most difficult decision came at the middle infield spots, where **Geraldo Perdomo** (45.25) was ultimately sidelined. Despite his speed profile, **Geraldo Perdomo** was excluded because he faces a formidable Gavyn Williams (2.99 xERA), which decimated his efficiency projection compared to **Luis Arraez** or **Gleyber Torres**. The primary risk today involves **Dylan Beavers** (53.37); while his 16% park factor is inviting, he is facing the daunting Zack Wheeler (2.88 xERA). His floor is protected by an elite batting order position, but the matchup against an ace makes him a volatile component of today\u2019s lineup. We will monitor the weather for **Cal Raleigh** (48.51) and **Daulton Varsho** (48.03), both of whom are hovering near the marginal threshold and face specific platoon or pitcher-skill headwinds that could turn them into liabilities if the conditions deteriorate.",
